Grant FireEye is a dwarf of the [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/Undercroft|Undercroft]] in [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/index|Iomenei]]. He is short and dense, and the lower half of his face is covered by a mask of the sort worn against bad air; his suit is welded and patched in places with different pieces of metal. In his left hand he carries a lantern that gives off a blue light, on his left arm a small buckler, and in his right a coiled metal whip that snaps out into a solid blade, and an eyepatch over one eye glows with light. He is called in to work in the dark, fume-filled parts of the tunnel.

He says he belongs to a religion that worships a polar bear god and a man named [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] who follows the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Judge of Ages|Judge]], and that anyone who sees one of them must give them everything they own. He carries healer's gloves though he is not trained in medicine.

He hunts the saboteur [[People/Gerhard|Gerhard]] with [[People/Barlow Crane|Barlow]] and [[People/Gage|Gage]].
